From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0033] meson-vdec: HEVC drain matches timestamps by offset

codec_hevc_show_frames() hands frames out with amvdec_dst_buf_done_offset() and
the frame's own stream offset, but __codec_hevc_flush_output() - the drain at
end of stream - used amvdec_dst_buf_done(), which pops the HEAD of the timestamp
list. The head is the CSD packet's record (VPS/SPS/PPS produce no picture), so
the first drained tail frame carried the finished CSD work's timestamp:

  DecodeComponent: Work with bitstreamId=0 not found, already abandoned?
  DecodeComponent: reportError(error=14)

Measured 23.09 with dectest on an 8 s x265 clip (200 frames, B-frames): kernel
#89 delivered 193/200 and failed the codec at EOS; with this patch (#90) 200/200,
bit-identical to c2.android.hevc.decoder, OUTPUT EOS reached.

---
diff -ruN s32/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c s33/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -714,7 +714,16 @@
 	struct hevc_frame *tmp, *n;
 
 	while ((tmp = codec_hevc_get_next_ready_frame(hevc))) {
-		amvdec_dst_buf_done(sess, tmp->vbuf, V4L2_FIELD_NONE);
+		/*
+		 * h96 0033 (23.09.2026): match by the frame's own stream offset,
+		 * exactly like codec_hevc_show_frames(). amvdec_dst_buf_done() pops
+		 * the HEAD of the timestamp list, and the head is the CSD packet's
+		 * record (VPS/SPS/PPS produce no picture): every drained tail frame
+		 * then carried the finished CSD work's timestamp, userspace answered
+		 * "Work with bitstreamId=0 not found" and failed the codec at EOS.
+		 */
+		amvdec_dst_buf_done_offset(sess, tmp->vbuf, tmp->offset,
+					   V4L2_FIELD_NONE, false);
 		tmp->show = 0;
 		hevc->frames_num--;
 	}
